  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency assistance for typhoon and flood-affected populations in South-Central Viet Nam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Between 16&#x2013;23 November 2025, consecutive typhoons caused severe flooding across South&#x2011;Central Viet Nam, affecting nearly 2 million people and damaging or inundating 495,000 homes. Dak Lak, Gia Lai, and Da Nang were among the hardest hit, where pre&#x2011;existing vulnerabilities among poor and ethnic minority households deepened the impact.As co&#x2011;chair of the Shelter/Non-Food Item (NFI) sector, IOM is supporting flood&#x2011;affected households in Dak Lak through targeted cash assistance for shelter repairs, essential NFIs, and urgent household needs.</narrative>
  </description>
